  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": null,
      "what": "This study quantifies the UAE's maritime energy demand and CO2 emissions through 2070 using historical bilateral trade data and Multi-Regional Input-Output modeling from the Global Energy and Climate Outlook 2024. It estimates that UAE trade-linked shipping emissions were 7.94 Mt CO2 in 2022, representing roughly 0.9% of the global international shipping total. Scenario analysis reveals that the nation's target of 75% ammonia fuel use by 2050 is unlikely to be met under current trends due to slow fleet turnover, high fuel costs, and lagging bunkering infrastructure.",
      "why": "It establishes a replicable national-level framework to test the feasibility of alternative fuel targets in international shipping, demonstrating that official decarbonization timelines are misaligned with actual fleet and infrastructure transition rates."
